n disqualified in 1948, this would have been the only circumstance in Olympic of the exact same team, with more than two members, winning the same event three consecutive times."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Germany won the silver medal in team dressage but did not closely challenge Sweden. The German team consisted of " [:a {:href "/athletes/11395"} "Liselott Linsenhoff"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/11505"} "Hannelore Weygand"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/11383"} "Anneliese Küppers"] ", a fully-female team for the first time in Olympic equestrian history. Switzerland won the bronze medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Team dressage was first placed on the Olympic Program in 1928. At Roma in 1960 the event would not be held, but it would return in 1964 and remain on the Olympic Program through 2012, and likely far longer."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Judge #1 Scores"] [:th {} "Judge #2 Scores"] [:th {} "Judges #3 Scores"] [:th {} "Judge #4 Scores"] [:th {} "Judge #5 Scores"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Sweden"] [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "2,475.00"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12678"} "Henri Saint Cyr"] " "] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/1289"} "Juli"]]] [:td {}] [:td {} "860.00"] [:td {} "160.0"] [:td {} "159.0"] [:td {} "192.0"] [:td {} "177.0"] [:td {} "172.0"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12557"} "Gehnäll Persson"] " "] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/1362"} "Knaust"]]] [:td {}] [:td {} "821.00"] [